mimalloc provides CMake targets:

  find_package(mimalloc CONFIG REQUIRED)
  target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE $<IF:$<TARGET_EXISTS:mimalloc-static>,mimalloc-static,mimalloc>)

To ensure the mimalloc.dll is loaded at runtime on Windows with
dynamic linkage, it is suggested to insert some call to the mimalloc API
in the main function, eg. `mi_version()`, or use the `/include:mi_version`
linker switch. Cf. https://github.com/microsoft/mimalloc#dynamic-override-on-windows
